  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find a past ticket reporting this same problem: Windows-to-WSL2 port forwarding over IPv4 loopback (127.0.0.1) failing after wsl --shutdown in NAT mode, while IPv6 (::1) still works. The closest tickets describe different problems. WSL#14154 is about dual-stack IPv6 sockets refusing IPv4 connections inside WSL. WSL#9750 is about forwarded ports disappearing a few seconds after a service starts. WSL#40688 is about NAT mode having no outbound connectivity at all. WSL#13868 is a mirrored-mode loopback issue. None of them gives a fix for your case. In the meantime, you can try connecting to localhost or ::1 (which already works for you), or to the WSL VM's eth0 IP address from Windows. Please file this as a new issue with the networking logs from collect-wsl-logs.ps1 -LogProfile networking attached.\"}",
